{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/904260-devilwhip-cosplay-prop-\u2013-requesting-feedback","id":904260,"title":"Devilwhip Cosplay Prop \u2013 Requesting Feedback","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-31T10:35:24-07:00","id":904260,"title":"Devilwhip Cosplay Prop \u2013 Requesting Feedback","content":"<span style=\"font-family:courier new\">I\u2019m working on a Devilwhip cosplay (not LARP) prop and looking for some feedback. A critique of something that only has one or two visual references is a little tricky, but maybe forumites will see something I\u2019m not.<br /> The primary visual inspiration for this is the depiction of the weapon Zyhzhak is wielding on the cover of <i>Book of the Wyrm</i> Second Edition. All constructive and honest opinions are welcome.<br /> For starters:</span><ul><li><span style=\"font-family:courier new\">Does it look like the tentacle of a demonic and lovecraftian personification of spiritual corruption?</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:courier new\">If you saw someone in werewolf makeup holding this, would you think \u201cblack spiral dancer\u201d? [I realize this depends on makeup, costume, and other props.]</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:courier new\">Are there details that I could add to give it more a \u201cbane tentacle\u201d vibe?</span></li> </ul><span style=\"font-family:courier new\">I'll post one image here and links to others below it. Thanks again for reading.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://i1373.photobucket.com/albums/ag389/Nazfool/Devilwhip/100_0796_zpsk6escc16.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://i1373.photobucket.com/albums/ag389/Nazfool/Devilwhip/100_0795_zpscdwhrejl.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">Devilwhip01</a><br /> <a href=\"http://i1373.photobucket.com/albums/ag389/Nazfool/Devilwhip/100_0798_zpszw4embbb.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">Devilship04</a><br /> <a href=\"http://i1373.photobucket.com/albums/ag389/Nazfool/Devilwhip/100_0797_zps6dvy0jxp.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">Devilwhip03</a><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">NOTE: This could be more of a MET sort of thing (idk), but I don\u2019t have a presence in the LARPing community.</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T13:04:30-07:00","id":904373,"title":"","content":"The only critique I have to offer is that the texture is undermining the &quot;bane tentacle&quot; effect. I have no idea what kind of resources you have, but from the pictures it looks like gaffer/electrical tape in a distracting sort of way.<br /> <br /> There's dozens of inspirations you could take from biology in terms of patterns, but some sort of skin on top of the current core could do wonders for adding that little touch. It will also help make the teeth look like natural outgrowths of a strange tentacle, instead of attached elements.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T14:50:31-07:00","id":904474,"title":"","content":"If you want to make it look more like an organic tentacle use some black liquid latex or plastidip and some gauze. Other then that, I think it looks fairly accurate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T01:19:10-07:00","id":904784,"title":"","content":"Hm, I think it could use some more weight and girth to it in addtion to giving it a biological texture. Like this it just looks like an ordinary whip with spikes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T01:52:07-07:00","id":904793,"title":"","content":"Gotta remember though that they have to carry that thing around too. A whole day of cosplay at a convention can make such a thing hellish.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T02:06:22-07:00","id":904794,"title":"","content":"We also don't have an exact scale.<br /> <br /> All the canon images of the devilwhip show it as fairly thin (at least compared to Zhyzhak in Homid). It's generally portrayed as being extremely long for a whip over being bulky and wide (some of the images of it would easily make it twice the length of a standard bullwhip; 8-10 feet for example are the lengths of the whips used in the Indiana Jones moves as a reference).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T17:39:10-07:00","id":905283,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:courier new\">Thank you, everyone. I appreciate all the ideas.</span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/904260-devilwhip-cosplay-prop-\u2013-requesting-feedback?p=904373#post904373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> \u2026but from the pictures it looks like gaffer/electrical tape in a distracting sort of way.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:courier new\">Damnit! You\u2019re totally right. I thought the same thing but I wasn\u2019t sure if that was me being overly critical. It is, in fact, electrical tape.</span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/904260-devilwhip-cosplay-prop-\u2013-requesting-feedback?p=904373#post904373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> \u2026some sort of skin on top of the current core could do wonders for adding that little touch. It will also help make the teeth look like natural outgrowths of a strange tentacle, instead of attached elements.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:courier new\">I was really hoping that the tape would have a millipede-skin-look, but it does need something else.</span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Derzhuzad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/904260-devilwhip-cosplay-prop-\u2013-requesting-feedback?p=904474#post904474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want to make it look more like an organic tentacle use some black liquid latex or plastidip and some gauze.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:courier new\">I thought about the liquid latex. I used a little on a much smaller proof-of-concept prop and it tended to crack with coiling and uncoiling. However, this plastidip stuff intrigues me. It looks reasonably priced and I think I might be able to find it locally. Thanks for the tip.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:courier new\">Regarding the scale and length:<br /> I was originally going to, as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1182_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1182\" data-vbnamecard=\"1182\">Asmodai</a> suggested, add some width and model it after a cephalopod tentacle. To make it coil-able, the taper would make it really, REALLY, long. Or it could be shorter, but in sketches in just looked comical.<br /> <br /> This prop is 10 feet long (about 3 meters). Described as 15 feet long (5-ish meters), the in-game Devilwhip feels like it should offer a considerable tactical advantage over a klaive, especially after messing with my \u201ctiny\u201d whip. Swinging it around outside feels like it should be a ranged weapon. /tangent<br /> <br /> Thanks again to everyone who responded. I have a few new ideas to move forward with. The invitation for feedback is still open.<br /> <br /> </span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T20:01:27-07:00","id":905347,"title":"","content":"So, an idea for faking the millipede thing:<br /> <br /> Millipedes have a series of segmented shells. That's pretty much not feasible for a project like this. But you can make the look stronger if you want to go this direction (this could be pretty tedious, but cosplay can do that):<br /> <br /> 1) The segments should be a bit &quot;bumpy&quot; and preferably with a bit of a taper. The thinner edge should be towards the tip, with the fattest part in biased towards the handle end, with a fairly quick drop off. Done in sequence down the line this should create the physical illusion of millipede segments. You could do this by wrapping more tape, or adding a stuffing layer, and covering it with tape The teeth should be spaced so they &quot;emerge&quot; between bumps, and the bumps should deform slightly where they extend out so it looks like they're growing out from underneath and between segments..<br /> <br /> 2) Millipedes have color. The primary shell color is black/brown, but there should be highlights at the edge of each segment. In many millipedes this is a neutral warm red/brown/yellow. Highly toxic millipedes usually advertise this via these highlights with very vibrant yellows, greens, or even pinks. Green is pretty appropriate for Zhyzhak of course. The bumble bee millipede or the yellow spotted millipede are two vibrant and basic patterns for how to add these sorts of colors (yellow spotted millipedes excrete cyanide... so their pattern is particularly strong on the &quot;hey I'm poison&quot; scale)..<br /> <br /> 3) Electrical tape is too matte for a millipede segment shells. It's made of the same materials as insect shells. For millipedes that rely on camouflage they're still matte, but less uniform. For warning coloration styles they're frequently a bit glossy; however that should be at the bulges of the segments more than at the joints. Obviously any paint needs to be something that can flex with the whip, but there's a few options there especially since you don't need a strong coating just enough to give it a sheen. This helps #1, and gives it a nice contrast that can help disguise the tape.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T21:27:19-07:00","id":905397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/904260-devilwhip-cosplay-prop-\u2013-requesting-feedback?p=905347#post905347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, an idea for faking the millipede thing: [String of awesome ideas]</div> </div> </div> </div> <span style=\"font-family:courier new\">That sounds brilliant and might be doable with what I have already. I think I\u2019m going to do two test sections. One with your segment-idea and another segment with some of the plastidip Derzhuzad mentioned. Either way, I love the idea of a little bit of toxic color. </span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T15:37:23-07:00","id":906755,"title":"","content":"I certainly wouldnt want to get hit by it! great job.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7706-somuchlove","name":"Somuchlove","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7706_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}